  "sn1.25:3.5": "This question confuses the conceit, “I am” <i>(asmimāna)</i> with the simple concept, “I.” The former is a fetter, in that it involves one in a tangle of views as to what the “I” is, and what it means to be. (See <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn2'>MN 2</a>.) The latter, as this verse shows, is simply a conventional expression, and if it can be separated from the conceit “I am,” it need not fetter the mind.",
